  "priorExpiration": "2009-11-11",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 5006.01 Record Required.\n\n(a) No person shall sell or transfer ownership of any display fireworks without making a record. The record shall be kept by the transferor for at least 5 years from the date of the sale.\n\n(b) The record in (a) above shall contain the following:\n\n(1) The name and address of the receiver;\n\n(2) The date of transfer;\n\n(3) The type and quantity of display fireworks sold;\n\n(4) The serial number and lot number of the display fireworks, if any; and\n\n(5) If the explosive material is to be used within the State of New Hampshire, the name and competency certificate number of the conductor of the display.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at Chapter Heading for Saf-C 5000) #6055, eff 7-1-95; amd by #7481, eff 4-25-01; paragraphs (b)(1)-(2) and (5) EXPIRED: 7-1-03; amd by #8117, INTERIM, eff 7-14-04; paragraphs (b)(1)-(2) and (5) EXPIRED: 1-10-05; amd by #8261, eff 1-21-05; amd by #9471, INTERIM, eff 5-15-09, EXPIRED: 11-11-09\n\nNew. #9765-A, eff 8-2-10; ss by #12124, eff 3-6-17",
